Due to being comprised entirely of nanites,{{Refn|[[:File:Upgrade Nanites 2.png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="Game Over">''[[Game Over]]''</ref> Upgrade is completely amorphous. His humanoid form can reshape and move like a liquid does.

Upgrade has the ability to merge with and possess any technology by encasing his liquified body over it. The size of the device is not significant and he controls it as naturally as he would his own body. When he merges, his black and green circuitry pattern spreads across the technology's surface to fit its proportions; although he also has the ability to perfectly replicate the technology's original colors.<ref>''[[Permanent Retirement]]''</ref><ref name="DAA">'''''[[Ben 10: Destroy All Aliens]]'''''</ref>

Upgrade can also telekinetically move and control any piece of technology he is possessing, but is not attached to his main body,<ref name="SZTWC">''[[Something Zombozo This Way Comes]]''</ref> even while possessing something else as well.<ref name="Framed">''[[Framed]]''</ref> He can also speak through what he is remotely possessing.<ref name="SZTWC" />

Upgrade's technological possession can work on non-electrical machinery, such as a row machine in a gym.<ref name="The Alliance">''[[The Alliance]]''</ref> His ability even extends to sentient beings that are mechanical in nature, like [[Chronosapien|Chronosapiens]];<ref>''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 1]]''</ref><ref>''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 2]]''</ref> or, at most, organic beings with some machinery integrated within them, such as [[Rojo]]<ref name="The Alliance" /> and [[Rex Salazar (Generator Rex)|Rex]].<ref name="Heroes United" />

Upgrade only needs a part (or extremity) of his body to touch a piece of technology to begin possessing it, as shown with the grapple cable of [[Rook Blonko|Rook]]'s [[Proto-Tool]].<ref name="SZTWC"/> He doesn't need to completely inhabit technology to begin possessing it, and can in fact phase right through them without disturbing the integrity of their surface, as shown with a [[Mechadroid#Basic Mechadroids|Mechadroid]]<ref name="Secrets">''[[Secrets]]''</ref> and Rex.<ref name="Heroes United" /> Upgrade can also make his head or face appear from anywhere on the machines he possesses.<ref name="Heroes United" />

Upgrade's DNA is "programmed" with blueprints and intimate knowledge of every alien technology.{{Refn|[[:File:Divided We Stand Pop-up (20).png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="DWS">''[[Divided We Stand]]''</ref> This allows him to enhance any tech he is possessing into "ultra-tech",{{Refn|[[:File:Upgrade Bandai Lenticular Card.png]]|group = Bandai|name = Bandai}} making it far more advanced and futuristic beyond [[Human (Classic)|human]] capability, and causing new features to form. After he separates from the machine, it returns to normal.

Upgrade can transform the technology he is possessing with seemingly no limit, such as upgrading a baseball pitching machine to produce a seemingly infinite number of baseballs;<ref>''[[Last Laugh]]''</ref> and transforming vehicles like the [[Rustbucket (Classic)|Rustbucket]] and [[Kevin's Car (Original)|Kevin's car]] into battle-ready machines and mecha-suits.<ref name="OTTO Motives">''[[OTTO Motives]]''</ref> He can also reconfigure his constructs at will to suit any situation, from summoning arsenals of heavy energy weapons and extra limbs, to changing their shape completely.<ref>''[[Road Trip Rumble]]''</ref> If Upgrade possesses a computer or control terminal, he can read local information from it, hack it, and manipulate it to execute commands as he wishes, even over entire networks. Upgrade has demonstrated this by assuming control of [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen's]] laptop;<ref name="Secrets" /> a video game console;<ref name="Game Over" /> and the entire [[Plumber Headquarters|Plumber Headquarters]].<ref name="TFC">''[[The Final Countdown]]''</ref> If given external empowerment, Upgrade can transport himself and organic creatures into the world of a video game, and vice versa. Whilst inside, he can change and manipulate the game's code just by thinking it.<ref name="Game Over" />

Once merged, Upgrade is capable of destroying and dismantling machines.<ref name="Secrets" /><ref name="Game Over" /> Upgrade can also repair damaged machinery with ease and come out unscathed, as demonstrated by [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]] when he used the [[Mechamorph Armor]] to absorb the pieces of the destroyed Rustbucket and reassemble them anew.<ref name="DAA" /> He is also able to restore manipulated or conjoined technologies back to their original states.<ref name="OTTO Motives" />

Due to his nanite liquid-like physiology, Upgrade can pass through all sorts of small spaces,<ref name="MM">''[[Midnight Madness]]''</ref> can be bisected any number of times with no harm done to him,<ref name="FHtE">''[[From Hedorium to Eternity]]''</ref> and easily rejoin any separated pieces of himself.<ref name="DAA" />

In his humanoid form, Upgrade is also very flexible, and can stretch himself very far. Upgrade was able to stretch his body's width to the point of acting like a parachute to save himself from a fall.<ref name="Secrets" /> He can also alter his own size, as demonstrated by a [[Mechamorph Guard]].<ref name="TUS">''[[The Ultimate Sacrifice]]''</ref> On top of modifying the shape of his humanoid form, Upgrade can extend from any part of his body cable or hand-like structures, as demonstrated by [[Malware]].<ref name="TH" /> Upgrade once used both of these powers to mimic the shape and body structure of a [[Tetramand (Classic)|Tetramand]], complete with the extra pair of arms.<ref name="DAA" />

Upgrade can use his shapeshifting to form various weapons and tools from his body, both while in his humanoid form or when possessing technology. He has been shown forming tentacles, spikes<ref name="Framed" /> and spiked maces.<ref name="Game Over" />

In having a vast library to draw upon, Upgrade may be able to mimic and shapeshift into technology without needing to possess it,{{Refn|[[:File:Upgrade Can Mimic Tech.png]]|group = DR}} as well as non-electrical items, as demonstrated by [[Ship]]<ref>''[[Pet Project]]''</ref> and a Mechamorph Guard.<ref name="TUS" />{{Refn|However, according to [[Derrick J. Wyatt]], Upgrade is not able to mimic technology{{Refn|[[:File:Upgrade Cannot Imitate Technology.png]]|group = DJW}} and that the Mechamorph Guard having the ability was a production error due to someone on the crew not having the basic understanding of how Upgrade works.{{Refn|[[:File:Upgrade Shapeshifting.png]]|group = DJW}}|group = note}}

Upgrade can generate solid constructs made of his nanites, such as pillars<ref name="TMTCP1" /> and spikes,<ref name="Showdown: Part 2">''[[Showdown: Part 2]]''</ref> as demonstrated by Malware.

By energizing his biomechanical blood,{{Refn|[[:File:Upgrade Plasma Beam.png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="Game Over" /> Upgrade can launch a powerful green plasma blast from his eye.<ref name="TT">''[[Tourist Trap]]''</ref><ref name="BAotD">''[[Be Afraid of the Dark]]''</ref><ref name="FHtE" /> The blast can also explode on contact or be made to create a delayed spherical explosion at their target destination, as demonstrated by other Galvanic Mechamorphs.<ref name="Showdown: Part 2" />

Upgrade can generate electrical charges capable of shocking his opponents into submission. He can also conduct these charges throughout his body.<ref name="DWS" /><ref name="Ken 10">''[[Ken 10]]''</ref>

Upgrade possesses enhanced strength, being able to throw a sewer lid at a [[Nosedeenian (Classic)|Nosedeenian]],<ref name="TT" /> push [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]] off of a [[Chimeran Hammer (Classic)|ship]],<ref name="Secrets" /> and overpower [[Dr. Viktor]].<ref name="BAotD" />

Upgrade is durable enough to withstand a blast from the Proto-Tool without physical damage.<ref name="SZTWC" />

Upgrade is very fast when running on all fours.<ref name="MM" />

Being inorganic, Upgrade is able to survive in the vacuum of space.<ref name="BAotD" /> Upgrade also doesn't need to breathe underwater, as shown by Malware.<ref name="TH" />

Upgrade is immune to being transformed into an [[Esoterica]] by [[Dagon]], and can use his body to shield others from the same, as demonstrated by Ship.<ref name="TUE1">''[[The Ultimate Enemy: Part 1]]''</ref> Upgrade is also resistant to fire and strong heat.<ref name="TH" />

Due to being technological, Upgrade possesses digitalized vision.<ref name="SE">''[[Side Effects]]''</ref> His circuitry also glows in the dark.<ref name="DAA" />

Upgrade is capable of transmitting distress signals, as demonstrated by Ship.<ref name="PP">''[[Pier Pressure]]''</ref> Upgrade is also able to store people or objects within his body, as demonstrated by Malware.<ref name="TH" /><ref name="Showdown: Part 2" />

Upgrade has the ability to manipulate the environment of Galvan B.<ref name="Showdown: Part 2">''[[Showdown: Part 2]]''</ref>

Upgrade is able to spawn smaller animalistic Mechamorphs, as shown when [[Baz-L]] spawned Ship.<ref name="PP" />

Upgrade can travel through electrical currents.<ref name="MM" />

Upgrade has also been shown generating energy-based constructs, such as a green energy spike<ref name="SE">''[[Side Effects]]''</ref> and a beam of light that can harm an [[Ectonurite (Classic)|Ectonurite]].<ref name="FHtE" /> Ship has been shown to able to track down the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] and [[Plumber Badge|Plumber Badges]].<ref name="PP" />{{Refn|However, it is unknown if Galvanic Mechamorphs naturally possess this ability, or if they need to possess technology to gain access to it.|group = note}}

