Upgrade's control over machines is not absolute, as sapient, intelligent machines like [[Slix Vigma]] can easily fight off Upgrade if he merges with them against their will.<ref name="GM">''[[Grudge Match]]''</ref> He may also be unable to override some security systems or combat computer viruses, such as those of the [[Megacruiser]]<ref name="GM" /> and [[Plumber Headquarters|Plumber Headquarters]], respectively.<ref name="TFC" />

Upgrade can be forcefully separated from technology, as demonstrated by [[Rojo]].<ref name="The Alliance" />

When possessing technology, Upgrade is able to falter in producing constructs exactly how he had envisioned them, seen when he upgraded an [[Urban Assault Vehicle|urban assault vehicle]] by adding even more guns to it.<ref name="DAA" />{{Refn|Though, it is unknown if this was caused by Upgrade making a mistake on his own, or if the vehicle's automated programming had any influence over him.|group = note}}

Upgrade can be hurt if he is pulled and stretched hard enough, as shown when he was being pulled and stretched by [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]]'s [[Mutant Sea Monster]].<ref name="DWS" />

Upgrade can be powered down by a [[Repo Boot]], as demonstrated with [[Ship]].<ref>''[[Don't Fear the Repo]]''</ref>

Upgrade is sensitive to electromagnetic pulses<ref>''[[Animo Crackers]]''</ref> and magnetic fields.<ref name="OB">''[[Outbreak]]''</ref>

Upgrade is vulnerable to having his energy absorbed, which leaves him petrified afterwards.<ref name="Showdown: Part 2" />

Being a swarm of nanomachines, Upgrade is weak against electricity, such as that generated by [[Nosedeenian (Classic)|Nosedeenians]],<ref name="TT" /> [[Cerebrocrustacean]]s<ref name="OB" /> and [[Conductoid]]s, the latter of which has been demonstrated with [[Malware]].<ref name="TMTCP1">''[[The More Things Change: Part 1]]''</ref>

Upgrade is weak against acid{{Refn|''[[Ben 10: The Complete Season 2]]''|group = AS}} and intense heat such as lava.{{Refn|[[:File:Upgrade Can Be Harmed By Lava.png]]|group = DJW}} This is because any sort of corrosive can upset his delicate chemistry.{{Refn|group = Bandai|name = Bandai}}

Upgrade can be controlled by [[Vladat]]s via their [[Corruptura]]s.{{Refn|[[:File:Whampire Can Control Mechamorphs.png]]|group = DJW}}

Upgrade can be trapped in crystals by [[Petrosapien (Classic)|Petrosapiens]], as demonstrated with Malware.<ref name="TH" />

Upgrade can be affected by technorganic viruses{{Refn|[[:File:Upgrade Techno Virus.png]]|group = DJW}} and a [[Nemuina]]'s sleeping dust.{{Refn|[[:File:Pesky Dust Can Affect Galvanic Mechamorphs and Polymorphs.PNG]]|group = DJW}}

Upgrade is vulnerable to being turned into a smoothie by [[Squirtapiller]]'s species.{{Refn|[[:File:Squirtapiller vs Polymorphs, Galvanic Mechamorphs and Lenopans.png]]|group = DJW}}

===Non-Canon Weaknesses===
